# MIRA Environment Configuration
# Template for the container's non-interactive first-boot env vars and the
# runtime feature switches. No script reads this file and `docker run` does
# not load it — pass the vars with `-e` / `--env-file` (container), or export
# them in the service environment (host install).
#
# If the first-boot vars are set, first-boot runs non-interactively.
# If omitted, run with:
#   docker run -it -v mira-data:/opt/vault -v mira-userdata:/opt/mira/app/data -v mira-pgdata:/var/lib/postgresql/17/main -v mira-valkey:/var/lib/valkey -p 1993:1993 mira:latest
# to get the interactive setup wizard.

# Required: OpenAI-compatible provider API key (default provider: Lunaroute —
# the same key can serve every route, incl. embeddings and the System One screen)
MIRA_PROVIDER_KEY=your-lunaroute-key-here

# Optional: Provider configuration (defaults to Lunaroute)
# MIRA_PROVIDER_NAME=Lunaroute
# MIRA_PROVIDER_ENDPOINT=https://gw.lunaroute.com/v1/chat/completions
# MIRA_PROVIDER_MODEL=

# Optional: Kagi search API key (kagi.com/settings?p=api)
# MIRA_KAGI_KEY=

# Optional: Injection-screen System One gateway token. Providing it enables
# the semantic injection screen (stored in Vault as systemone_key); without
# it the screen stays off and external content is structurally wrapped only.
# MIRA_SYSTEMONE_API_KEY=

# Optional: Custom database password (defaults to internal default)
# MIRA_DB_PASSWORD=

# Optional: cognitive feature switches (strict 0 or 1; any other value fails at config load)
# Set to 0 to bypass subcortical memory surfacing and complexity assessment.
# MIRA_SUBCORTICAL_ENABLED=1
# Set to 0 to omit the Peanut Gallery observer, trinket, and event subscriber.
# MIRA_PEANUTGALLERY_ENABLED=1
# Set to 0 to omit Persona: the trinket, the segment-evaluation and refinement pass on
# collapse, and the persona/* actions. The user model (behavioral_directives) is
# unaffected by this switch.
# MIRA_PERSONA_ENABLED=1

# Optional: the first name the container's single-mode local account is created with —
# what MIRA calls you in its welcome messages and orientation memory. Defaults to "Friend".
# MIRA_LOCAL_SESSION_FIRST_NAME=Taylor

# Optional: request sizing. Deploy resolves these from the chosen chat endpoint's models
# list (live compaction fires at 80% of the window); set them by hand only for an endpoint
# that does not report a window. Both must be positive integers, compaction below window.
# MIRA_CONTEXT_WINDOW_TOKENS=200000
# MIRA_COMPACTION_TRIGGER_TOKENS=160000
